{
  "start": "-P14D",
  "periodOverride": "inherit",
  "widgets": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 24,
      "height": 3,
      "properties": {
        "markdown": "# Lost Together - experiment and site health\nSimulated lost hikers share a living map built from what each sees while an uncertain predator hunts them. Each bar is one (sweep, perception, predator, cooperation) group published by `infra/aws/publish_metrics.py` from a sweep CSV. **Escape rate** = mean share of hikers who escaped; **Δ vs solo** = paired-by-seed difference in percentage points (same forest, spawns and predator start). Everything shown is simulated; the Perception dimension says which tier (surrogate or pixels) produced it. Bars average every publish of a sweep in the last 14 days, so republish a corrected sweep under a new name."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "metric",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3,
      "width": 12,
      "height": 6,
      "properties": {
        "title": "Escape rate by cooperation mode (%)",
        "view": "bar",
        "region": "ap-south-1",
        "stacked": false,
        "metrics": [
          [
            {
              "expression": "SEARCH('{LostTogether,Cooperation,Perception,Predator,Sweep} MetricName=\"EscapeRate\"', 'Average', 86400)",
              "id": "e1",
              "label": ""
            }
          ]
        ],
        "setPeriodToTimeRange": true,
        "period": 86400,
        "stat": "Average",
        "yAxis": {
          "left": {
            "min": 0,
            "max": 100,
            "label": "% hikers escaped",
            "showUnits": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "metric",
